# Q8 — "order these triggers" without full control, and the real ordering ask
# with it. NOT VERIFIED — see `wave33-evidence/s3-blockers.md`, "Q8" for the
# full account. Two designs were tried against a real match and neither got
# seat 0's life to actually drop (the one observable proof the Dark Confidant
# triggers fired at all):
#   1. `activephase=UPKEEP` + `activephaseadvance=UPKEEP` (a synthetic jump):
#      `GameState`'s general phase-advance has no equivalent to
#      `handleCombat`'s own `addAllTriggeredAbilitiesToStack()` call, so the
#      trigger condition is registered but never materialised onto the stack.
#   2. This file's current shape — landing in the OPPONENT's Cleanup Step and
#      driving Cleanup→Untap→Upkeep→Draw→Main1→Combat through ordinary
#      priority passes (the same mechanism every real game uses): life was
#      STILL 20 by the time the drive reached seat 0's Declare Attackers
#      Step. Whether that is this scenario genuinely not producing the
#      triggers, or a flaw in the test's own drive loop (pressing every
#      `Priority:` window blindly, which could race past the one upkeep
#      stop that mattered before anything inspected it), was not resolved
#      within budget. No `.jvm.test.ts` exercises this file — do not assume
#      it works.
turn=1
activeplayer=ai
activephase=CLEANUP
humanlife=20
ailife=20
humanhand=
humanbattlefield=Dark Confidant;Dark Confidant
humanlibrary=Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain
humangraveyard=
aihand=
aibattlefield=
ailibrary=Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain;Mountain
